# Refresh Threadfin live-only M3U from Xtream Codes API nightly at 23:45.
# Pulls current live streams from provider and rebuilds the channel list at
# /srv/docker/threadfin/conf/live_only.m3u, which Threadfin then ingests during
# its own scheduled update at 00:00 (settings.json "update": ["0000"]).
# The 15-minute lead matters: at the old 04:00 slot Threadfin had already read
# the previous day's file four hours earlier, so the refresh never reached Plex.
45 23 * * * python3 /srv/docker/threadfin/conf/generate_live_m3u.py >> /home/jay/logs/threadfin-m3u.log 2>&1

# Fleet-wide permissions forensic monitor, every 15 minutes. Scans /mnt/media for
# files at mode 000 (unreadable, even by owner) or mode 777 (unexpectedly
# permissive), logs a forensic detail block for any newly-seen file to
# /home/jay/logs/permissions-forensics.log, and queues it in
# /home/jay/logs/permissions-pending-fixes.txt. Alert-first, never auto-fixes —
# run permissions-apply-fix.sh by hand after reviewing the queue. Replaces the
# retired zero-perm-subtitle-monitor.sh, which only ever covered subtitle files.
*/15 * * * * /home/jay/mediahub-configs/scripts/permissions-monitor.sh

# Internet connection monitor (latency every run; upload/download tests only when no remote Plex stream is playing).
# Logs to ~/logs/netmon/ (outside the repo: contains the public IP). Report: scripts/netmon-report.py. docs/netmon.md
*/30 * * * * flock -n /tmp/netmon.lock /home/jay/mediahub-configs/scripts/netmon.py >> /home/jay/logs/netmon/cron.log 2>&1  # internet monitor, see docs/netmon.md
* * * * * /home/jay/mediahub-configs/scripts/netmon.py --sample >> /home/jay/logs/netmon/cron.log 2>&1  # netmon 1-minute load+latency sampler, see docs/netmon.md
